/* SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
 * Provenance: original pcrec-memory-functions text; no third-party source
 *   (memfn/PROVENANCE.md).
 *
 * memfn/src/levels.def — THE KIT'S ISA LEVELS (R4e' batch 1, request R-13;
 * docs/design/memfn/integration.md §R4.9.2.2; unit U2, R-37, the guard
 * column became `needs`). An X-macro in options.def's idiom, kit-private:
 * pcrec's build never reads it and pcrec's sources never include it (C4).
 * The ONE place a level is named: a SIMD row references a level by token and
 * never names a feature; the seam (ofsskip.c) writes each level's include
 * from these strings; the tests read them through mf_levels().
 *
 * MF_LEVEL(token, family, needs, header, vw, test_march, forbid, stamp)
 *   token       kit-private id (an enum in kit.h, in this file's order)
 *   family      the family token (targets.def's MF_FAMILY name) the level's
 *               text is for
 *   needs       the FEATURE TOKENS (targets.def's vocabulary, sorted,
 *               comma-separated) the level's text needs (unit U2, R-37;
 *               target_seam.md §3): a level is ADMITTED for an art whose
 *               stated target (mf_art_target) is of the level's family and
 *               supplies every need among its features (levels.c,
 *               kit_target_levels). A FACT, no spelling: the C text carries no
 *               CPU #if (the guard column it replaced); the target's REGION,
 *               which pcrec places around the part, supplies the ISA. The
 *               table check (memfn/tests/check_targets.sh) holds admission
 *               to the compiler: a need is supplied by a target iff adding
 *               it to `-march=<target>` changes no macro
 *   header      the compiler header the level's text includes, once per
 *               artifact ([r9 C-7, F-10]: a compiler header, not a libc one,
 *               so the artifact stays self-contained), inside the region with
 *               the rest of the text (target_seam.md §3, F10)
 *   vw          the register width in bytes, the DERIVED vector width (D149)
 *   test_march  the TARGET token the kit's tests compile the level at (also
 *               gcc's -march name; [r9 F-13]); the level is admitted there
 *   forbid      instruction classes (kit.h MF_I_*) a row at this level may
 *               NOT use until a pcrec-bench run on Zen 1 shows no loss
 *               ([r9 M-11]): PDEP/PEXT (microcoded on Zen 1) and gathers
 *   stamp       the level's token in MEMFN_FORMS and in a helper's name
 *               (`<fn>__<stamp>`), opaque and arch-blind
 *
 * ORDER: ascending width. The seam writes level blocks in this order (each
 * helper defined before the one that falls through to it) and calls the top
 * admitted one from the selector. A target admitting the w32 level admits
 * the w16 level too (the table check holds it for the family's targets), so
 * a w32 helper's fall-through to w16 always names a defined function.
 * A level adds its gate class (fields.def's NO_<token>) by this row alone.
 * A 64-byte level and every arm64 level are born with their first row
 * (§R4.9.7's filed list).
 */
MF_LEVEL(LV_X86_W16, "amd64", "sse2", "emmintrin.h", 16, "x86-64",
         MF_I_PDEP_PEXT | MF_I_GATHER, "w16")
MF_LEVEL(LV_X86_W32, "amd64", "avx2", "immintrin.h", 32, "x86-64-v3",
         MF_I_PDEP_PEXT | MF_I_GATHER, "w32")
